course: dictionary
lesson: 3036
title: Many meanings, one word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. «Earmark» is one of them. Context tells you which meaning fits. Read the words around it and ask what they are about: money, animals, or a book.
explain: As a verb, to earmark means to set money or something aside for a special purpose. «The money is earmarked for a new playground.» That money is kept for the playground and cannot be spent on anything else. Earmarked is the past form and earmarking is the -ing form.
explain: As a noun, an earmark is a mark cut or tagged on a farm animal's ear to show who owns it. Another noun meaning is a sign or feature that shows what something is. «It has all the earmarks of a good book» means it shows the signs of being a good book.
fact: Earmark (verb) means to set money or something aside for one special purpose.
fact: «The money is earmarked for a new playground» means that money is kept for the playground only.
fact: An earmark (noun) is a mark or tag on a farm animal's ear that shows who owns it.
fact: «Have all the earmarks of» means show all the signs of: «It has all the earmarks of a good book.»
fact: In the US, «earmarks» can mean money set aside for a politician's favourite projects in his own local area.
exercise: «The money is earmarked for a new playground.» What does earmarked mean here? | *Set aside for one special purpose | Spent on sweets at the shop | Lost under the sofa | Given back to the bank
exercise: A farmer checks the earmark on a sheep's ear. What does the earmark show? | What the sheep likes to eat | How old the sheep is | *Who owns the sheep | Whether the sheep is hungry
exercise: «It has all the earmarks of a good book.» What does earmarks mean here? | Money paid for the book | Marks cut into the pages | Tags for a library | *Signs or features that show what something is
test: «The school fund is earmarked for new computers.» What is the fund kept for? | Lunches for everyone | *Only new computers | A trip to the zoo | Books for the library
test: «The bruise on his knee had all the earmarks of a fall from a bike.» What does this mean? | It was painted on for a play | He had just bought a new bike | *It showed the signs of a fall from a bike | It was caused by a football
exam: Which sentence uses earmark as a verb? | The farm's earmarks were checked each spring | The mark had all the earmarks of a fake | The sheep had a new earmark on its ear | *The council earmarked the spare money for a swimming pool
